WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.830
Film Courage:&nbsp; Clive, you say you’re attracted
to dangerous characters, how does Walt (of

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.830
THE CONFIRMATION) fit into that?

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:06.830
Clive Owen:&nbsp; Do I say that?

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.740
Film Courage: Well….I think your IMDB says
it?

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.430
Clive Owen: (Laughs) No, I wouldn’t say
I’m attracted to dangerous characters.&nbsp;

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:22.220
I’m attracted to characters that have conflicts,
because for me, it’s always more interesting

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.050
than a character that hasn’t got conflict
and it’s more real.&nbsp;

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.880
So, a character that is grappling with something
is always much more interesting to play because

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.002
you’ve got more than one thing to play all
the time and this film (THE CONFIRMATION)

00:00:33.002 --> 00:00:37.949
certainly falls into that bracket because
he’s a father, estranged from his son who

00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:41.269
is trying to make a go of it, and trying to
do the right thing and it’s very difficult

00:00:41.269 --> 00:00:46.210
in his circumstances and he’s got certain
demons he’s dealing with.&nbsp;

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:52.079
So it certainly falls into the bracket of
a character in conflict.Film Courage:&nbsp; Sure…..but

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:53.089
he’s redeemable?

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:54.589
Clive Owen:&nbsp; Yeah….

00:00:54.589 --> 00:00:59.260
At the end of the day his (Walt in THE CONFIRMATION)
intentions are true and good and he’s trying

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.729
to make a go of it, but it’s not always
easy.&nbsp;

00:01:01.729 --> 00:01:04.909
One thing that is very sweet about this film
is it’s about a group of characters living

00:01:04.909 --> 00:01:08.710
in a particular area and a lot of them have
a very tough time and are struggling, but

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:11.200
it’s very non-judgmental.&nbsp;

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.420
It’s not a film that looks down on these
people.&nbsp;

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.280
It’s a film that you kind of have empathy
and understand how hard it is for a lot of

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.280
people.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.280
Film Courage:&nbsp; Sure.&nbsp;

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.399
I grew up with a single parent and could relate
to a lot of the scenes in the film.&nbsp;

00:01:23.399 --> 00:01:26.950
Jaeden for you, how did you prepare for your
character, Anthony?&nbsp;

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.880
Did you go into what his life would be like,
especially for some of the scenes like sitting

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.729
in the truck outside the bar?

00:01:35.729 --> 00:01:43.929
Jaeden Lieberher:&nbsp; He (Anthony) is this good
kid.&nbsp;

00:01:43.929 --> 00:01:51.160
He doesn’t usually get into trouble until
he’s with his Dad.&nbsp;

00:01:51.160 --> 00:02:00.520
He’s very curious about the world and what
his father is dealing with.&nbsp;

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.929
I had to do the same thing.&nbsp;

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:17.130
I had to think about the different things
that was going on with my father and what

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:24.640
would think about during a moment where he
was in this truck all alone.&nbsp;

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.290
I had to think about what Anthony would be
thinking.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.420
Film Courage:&nbsp; Jaeden, you are 13 now?

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.340
Jaeden Lieberher:&nbsp; I am 13, yes.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:37.170
Film Courage:&nbsp; Ok…What would you recommend
to another 13-year-old on getting into the

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.650
(acting) business?

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:47.210
Jaeden Lieberher:&nbsp; Well….of course, I couldn’t
have gotten into “the business” if I didn’t

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:56.640
know anybody and just having this interest
in acting….

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:03.450
And if you don’t want to act, you don’t
necessarily have to, but it’s something

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.600
that you do, if you truly to do it.&nbsp;

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:15.610
So if you’re interested by acting and you’re
interested in being someone else, then you

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.210
should definitely pursue it.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.590
Film Courage:&nbsp; (To Jaeden) And you also want
to direct one day?

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.350
Jaeden Lieberher:&nbsp; I would like to direct
one day.&nbsp;

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:28.700
That is why I’m so happy that I was able
to work with Bob (Nelson) and everybody else.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.410
Film Courage:&nbsp; Did the two of you direct
each other at any point?

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:37.980
Clive Owen:&nbsp; Wouldn’t dream of it…..wouldn’t
dream of it (laughs).

